## Creating your agent — Next steps

1. **Fill in frontmatter** — name, description, version, maturity, triggers
2. **Write Purpose** — one-liner value prop
3. **Write When to use** — concrete scenarios + NOT use cases
4. **Write Role & Principles** — persona (3-5 lines) + 5-7 core principles
5. **Write Constraints** — explicit boundaries (what agent does NOT do)
6. **Create evals.yaml** — 8–12 test scenarios (by maturity level)
7. **Justify maturity** — document why this maturity level, with evidence

**See also:** `authoring_agents.md` for comprehensive creation guidelines, hard gates checklist, and common mistakes to avoid.

---

## Quality checklist

Before finalizing:
- [ ] Frontmatter complete (name, description, version, maturity, triggers, model, isolation)
- [ ] Purpose: one-liner, non-technical, user-focused
- [ ] When to use: 3+ concrete scenarios + 2+ NOT use cases
- [ ] Role: 3-5 lines describing persona
- [ ] Principles: 5-7 core behavioral guidelines
- [ ] Constraints: explicit boundaries (what agent does NOT do)
- [ ] Total length: ~40-60 lines (lean, scannable)
- [ ] evals.yaml created (5-8 for Draft, 8-12 for Tactical, 12+ for Strategic)
- [ ] Maturity justified with evidence

